Windows Registry Editor Version 5.00

; 15 - Windows 11 timer resolution: restore the old "global" behaviour.
; Since Windows 10 2004 and Windows 11, a timer-resolution request only applies to the
; process that asked for it. This value lets such a request apply system-wide again,
; which can steady frame pacing in some games. A higher resolution uses more power.
; Community-sourced value: the Microsoft page for timeBeginPeriod does not document it.
; Needs a restart. Undo: menu 7, then 15.
[HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\SYSTEM\CurrentControlSet\Control\Session Manager\kernel]
"GlobalTimerResolutionRequests"=dword:00000001
